Author: Seth Junot <xsetech@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Feb 20 04:24:48 2026 -0800

    fix: restore CPU allocator after allocator tests to prevent dangling pointer
    
    SaveAndLoadWithAllocator and LoadWithMultiThreadsWithAllocator both set
    the global CPU allocator to a local TestAllocator instance via
    SetCPUAllocator. When the test ends the local goes out of scope, leaving
    a dangling pointer in the global allocator registry. The subsequent test
    then calls GetCPUAllocator(), receives that dangling pointer, and uses it
    as the base for its own TestAllocator, causing a segfault on the first
    virtual call through the stale vtable.
    
    Fix by restoring the original allocator at the end of each test using
    the same priority (10) so the SetAllocator priority-gate is satisfied.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/caffe2/serialize/inline_container_test.cc b/caffe2/serialize/inline_container_test.cc
index 489751522fb..c6531eb956c 100644
--- a/caffe2/serialize/inline_container_test.cc
+++ b/caffe2/serialize/inline_container_test.cc
@@ -532,6 +532,9 @@ TEST(PyTorchStreamWriterAndReader, SaveAndLoadWithAllocator) {
   EXPECT_EQ(baseAllocator.getAllocatedBytes(), allocBytes + kBytes1 + kBytes2);
   std::tie(data_ptr, size) = reader.getRecord("key2", &baseAllocator);
   EXPECT_EQ(baseAllocator.getAllocatedBytes(), allocBytes + kBytes1 + 2 * kBytes2);
+
+  // Restore the original CPU allocator so it doesn't dangle after this test.
+  c10::SetCPUAllocator(defaultAllocator, 10 /* priority */);
 }
 
 
@@ -624,6 +627,9 @@ TEST(PyTorchStreamWriterAndReader, LoadWithMultiThreadsWithAllocator) {
   }
   // clean up
   remove(file_name);
+
+  // Restore the original CPU allocator so it doesn't dangle after this test.
+  c10::SetCPUAllocator(defaultAllocator, 10 /* priority */);
 }
 
 class ChunkRecordIteratorTest : public ::testing::TestWithParam<int64_t> {};
